  "caseId": "case08",
  "description": "Two consecutive account breaks, and the off-by-one that is CORRECT. Three accounts with one category each, every balance 1000.00 at fifteen percent, so each accrues exactly 12.50. The break at record 2 rewrites account 1 (194.00 -> 206.50) and the break at record 3 rewrites account 2 (158.00 -> 170.50), while ACCOUNT 3 IS NEVER REWRITTEN and keeps its seeded 147.00. Three accounts, two rewrites: the ELSE at :219-221 that would flush the final group cannot run, because PERFORM UNTIL END-OF-FILE = 'Y' has already established that the flag is not 'Y' and 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT moves nothing but 'Y' into it. That is the legacy behaviour and this case is the one that would fail loudest if somebody added an end-of-file flush to 'fix' it - which would alter the account master on every run.",
